# These repositories are developed on Windows, macOS and Linux, but the daemon,
# container entrypoints, udev rules, systemd units and shell scripts are all
# consumed by Linux at runtime. Normalize every text file to LF both in the
# object store and on checkout, so no contributor's platform, client config, or
# editor can introduce CRLF.
#
# This is not cosmetic. A CRLF container entrypoint fails at startup with a
# confusing "exec format error", and CRLF shell scripts make ShellCheck report
# thousands of spurious SC1017 "literal carriage return" findings that bury the
# real ones. Both have happened here.
#
# Covers extensionless executables too (scripts/backup/mochad-redux-backup,
# packaging/openwrt/*), which are text but easy to miss in a rule keyed on
# file extension.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images must never be newline-converted or line-diffed.
*.png binary
